I fear in my brief absence a harmless suggestion has polymorphed into a
vicious debate over the Nature of Nethack.  There are so many things in
Nethack, that, if it was a strict period piece, would seem totally
bizarre.  Like that scene in Ninja Scroll 2 where that thin guy pulls
out a SAM missle launcher and starts lobbing rockets at Jubei; I mean come
on!  For some Reason we don't react the same way when we use a magic
marker or, for that matter, kill a grid bug (inter-dimensional travel is
impossible!).  Maybe it's because Ninja Scroll 2 sucked, and Nethack is
one of the best games ever made.  When we see something unrealistic in a
crappy anime like NS2, it just gives us more reason to hate it.  When we
see something unrealistic in Nethack, it just gives us more reason to love
the DevTeam, for their innovativeness and willingness to try something out
there, but totally cool.

